<article class="env-definition" id="06ZL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06ZL">Definition <span data-tag="06ZL">35.12.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\tau \in \{ Zar, {\acute{e}tale}, smooth, syntomic, fppf\} $. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a presheaf of $\mathcal{O}$-modules on $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_\tau $. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is called <em>parasitic</em><a class="footnotemark" href="#a0000771625" id="a0000771625-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> if for every flat morphism $U \to S$ we have $\mathcal{F}(U) = 0$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\mathcal{F}$ is called <em>parasitic for the $\tau $-topology</em> if for every $\tau $-covering $\{ U_ i \to S\} _{i \in I}$ we have $\mathcal{F}(U_ i) = 0$ for all $i$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>